-- title:
--   Descent of level automorphisms to F̄ at q=2
-- statement:
--   Let $q$ be a prime with $q=2$, let $M'$ be a nonzero natural number with $q \nmid M'$, and let $\ell_g$ be a prime with $\ell_g \equiv 11 \pmod{12}$ and $\ell_g \mid M'$; assume $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldBar}\,M' \le \mathrm{fieldBar}\,q\,M'$, i.e. the coefficientwise base change to $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ of the full level-$M'$ modular function field lies in $\mathrm{fieldBar}\,q\,M' = \mathrm{xHFunctionFieldBar}\,(q^2M')\,(\mathrm{levelH}\,q\,M')$. Let $k_0$ be an intermediate field of $\overline{\mathbb Q}/\mathbb Q$ containing a primitive $q$-th root of unity $\xi$. Put $H_1 = \mathrm{levelH}\,q\,M' \sqcap \ker\big((\mathbb Z/q^2M')^\times \to (\mathbb Z/\ell_g)^\times\big)$, where $\mathrm{levelH}\,q\,M'$ is the kernel of the unit reduction out of modulus $q^2M'$ named by `dvd_sq_mul q M'`; let $K = \mathrm{laurentBaseChange}\,k_0\,(\mathrm{xHFunctionField}\,(q^2M')\,H_1)$, the subfield of $\mathrm{LaurentSeries}\,k_0$ generated over $k_0$ by the coefficientwise image of that function field; let $G \le \mathrm{Aut}(K/k_0)$ be generated by all $\tau$ for which some $\gamma \in \Gamma(q) \cap \Gamma_0(M')$ satisfies $\mathrm{IsLevelAutAt}\,k_0\,q\,\xi\,q\,(q^2M')\,H_1\,\gamma^{-1}\,K\,\tau$ (that is, $\tau$ carries every ratio of integral $q$-expansions of weight-$k$ forms on $\Gamma_{H_1}(q^2M')$ to the corresponding ratio after slashing by $\mathrm{conjElemN}\,q\,\gamma^{-1}$, under any embedding $k_0 \to \mathbb C$ sending $\xi$ to $e^{2\pi i/q}$), and let $K_0$ be the fixed field of $G$. Give $\mathrm{fieldBar}\,q\,M'$ the $k_0$-algebra structure obtained from $k_0 \hookrightarrow \overline{\mathbb Q}$. Then for every intermediate field $F_0$ of $\mathrm{fieldBar}\,q\,M'/k_0$ whose members are exactly the elements all of whose Laurent coefficients lie in the image of $k_0$, and every $k_0$-algebra isomorphism $\varphi : K_0 \simeq F_0$ which is coefficientwise compatible (the image of $f$ under $\mathrm{coeffMap}$ along $k_0 \to \overline{\mathbb Q}$ is the Laurent series of $\varphi f$), the following holds: for every $\zeta : \mathrm{Idx}\,q$, every primitive $q$-th root of unity $\xi' \in k_0$ whose image in $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ is $\zeta$, every $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$ and every $\tau \in \mathrm{Aut}(K/k_0)$ with $\mathrm{IsLevelAutAt}\,k_0\,q\,\xi'\,q\,(q^2M')\,H_1\,\gamma\,K\,\tau$, the automorphism $\tau$ maps $K_0$ into itself, and $\varphi(\tau f) = (\mathrm{levelAutBar}\,q\,M'\,\zeta\,\gamma)(\varphi f)$ for all $f \in K_0$.
--
--   This is the transport step of the diamond-operator frame at $q = 2$: the level automorphisms of the auxiliary field $K$ at level $\Gamma_{H_1}(q^2M')$, with the rigidifying prime $\ell_g \equiv 11 \pmod{12}$ dividing $M'$ in place of an auxiliary full level, are shown to preserve the fixed field $K_0 = K^G$ and to correspond, under the coefficientwise identification $\varphi$ with $F_0$, to the chosen automorphisms $\mathrm{levelAutBar}\,q\,M'\,\zeta\,\gamma$ of $\mathrm{fieldBar}\,q\,M'$. It feeds the construction of the Galois-equivariant identification of $K_0$ with the level field used to define the diamond action.
